| `import_layers.may_end_the_process.<name>` | string | `scripts/jobs/conflict_guard.py`, with the reason that it runs before its importer can hold a `main`; absent, `{}`, announced as `[using default] import_layers.may_end_the_process = {}` | a repo-relative module path mapped to a non-blank reason | `tests/source_tree.py` (`import_layers`); `tests/integration/test_exit_gate.py` (`library_findings`) | Lets the named module, which other project modules import, end the process through `fail` or `finish` outside an entry block. An entry naming no imported module that does fails the gate test, and so does a blank reason. | a script's own entry block, which may always call `finish` | always |
